eturn self.monsters.get((x, y))\n    def remove_monster(self, x, y):\n        if (x, y) in self.monsters:\n            del self.monsters[(x, y)]\n\n\nentities.py\npython\n\'\'\'\nEntity classes for the player, monsters, and treasure chests.\n\'\'\'\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n@dataclass\nclass Player:\n    x: int\n    y: int\n    hp: int = 100\n@dataclass\nclass Monster:\n    x: int\n    y: int\n    hp: int\n@dataclass\nclass Chest:\n    x: int\n    y: int\n    heal: int\n\n\n'} |
